 "result_text": "I added a \"Delete All\" button to the contents view. It deletes every item in the folder, not just the 1,000 shown on the current page. I only checked that the module imports; I didn't click the button in a running Zope or add tests.\n\n- **Method:** `manage_delAllObjects` in `BTreeFolder2.py` collects every id with `objectIds()` and passes them to the standard `manage_delObjects`. It then redirects back to `manage_main`. It requires the \"Delete objects\" permission.\n- **Button:** `contents.dtml` shows the button next to \"Delete\", inside the same permission check. It asks for confirmation first (\"Delete ALL items in this folder?\").\n\nAll ids are deleted in a single request, so a folder with a very large number of items could make that request slow or memory-heavy.",
